{=============================================================================
  Cogeneration monthly balance and annual demand (exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0233
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  MSTh repetition, exercise 2 (file MSTH051213, 2005-12-13). The window
  computes a monthly balance for November and December: capacity rate,
  slope, heat demand, captured heat and backup energy, then the annual
  demand. Temperatures t_nov and t_dec are assigned and unused elsewhere.
  The intersection notes 350 and 200 are comments; those numbers already
  sit in the captured-heat equations. December backup uses 30 days.
  No fluid, no property call, and no diagram-state array. Not an exam.

  Inputs : M_dot, c_w, A, t_nov, t_dec, and the demand and capture equations
  Outputs: Q_dot_appoint_kWh_mois_nov, Q_dot_appoint_kWh_dec, Q_demande_kWh_an
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
           (the kWh results stay as written; nothing is rescaled)
  Source : ULiège MSTh, MSTH051213 EXERCICE 2.EES; the equation window
           names nobody - see README.md
  Licence: MIT. Status: verified against the EES stored solution.
=============================================================================}

"!Data"
"MSTH051213 exercise 2, as in the original."
M_dot = 150/(24*3600)                                          "mass flow rate [kg/s]; 150/(24*3600) as in the original"
C_dot = M_dot*c_w                                              "capacity rate [W/K]"
c_w = 4187                                                     "specific heat [J/kg-K]; an equation, as in the original"
pente = C_dot*24/A                                             "slope [W/K]; 24/A as written"
A = 5                                                          "A, as in the original"
"As in the original: one finds pente = 34.89."

"!November"
"November, as in the original."
t_nov = 5.5                                                    "November temperature [°C]; no other equation uses it"
"Intersection: 350, as in the original."

"!Monthly balance"
"Monthly balance, as in the original."
Q_dot_demande = C_dot*(55-10)                                  "demand heat rate [W]; (55-10) as in the original"
Q_dot_capté_nov = 350*(A/24)                                   "captured heat rate in November [W]; 350 already in this equation"
Q_dot_appoint_nov = Q_dot_demande-Q_dot_capté_nov              "backup heat rate in November [W] (appoint)"
Q_dot_appoint_kWh_mois_nov = Q_dot_appoint_nov*30*24/1000      "backup energy in November [kWh]; 30 days as in the original"
eta_nov = Q_dot_capté_nov/Q_dot_demande                        "November ratio of captured heat to demand [-]"

"!December"
"December, as in the original."
t_dec = 3.5                                                    "December temperature [°C]; no other equation uses it"
"Intersection: 200, as in the original."
Q_dot_capté_dec = 200*(A/24)                                   "captured heat rate in December [W]; 200 already in this equation"
Q_dot_appoint_dec = Q_dot_demande-Q_dot_capté_dec              "backup heat rate in December [W] (appoint)"
Q_dot_appoint_kWh_dec = Q_dot_appoint_dec*30*24/1000           "backup energy in December [kWh]; 30 days as in the original"
eta_dec = Q_dot_capté_dec/Q_dot_demande                        "December ratio of captured heat to demand [-]"

"!Annual demand"
"Annual demand in kWh, as in the original."
Q_demande_kWh_an = Q_dot_demande*365*24/1000                   "annual demand [kWh]; 365 days as in the original"
